          "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A7-95",
          "body": "> can you clarify what \"didn't allow\" means? did you get an error from the orbic installer or was there no wifi network to begin with?\r\n\r\nThe installer failed, sorry. It allowed connection to the network, but wouldn't pull anything up with 192.168.1.1 nor communicate properly via the installer in powershell. I tried Windows and Linux, it seemed that adb was broken - adb reboot bootloader, setprop and similar didn't work and gave access denied errors. It seemed that the firmware was in a weird state where it didn't respond properly and was only fixed by counter-intuitively updating the firmware",
